      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1780754885083,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n1) Functional Requirements:  \n- Users can send and receive messages in 1:1 and group chats (ordered,\npersistent history).\n- Messages support rich media (images, videos, files).\n- Users receive real-time in-app and push notifications for new\nmessages.\n- Users can delete their own messages, reflecting across all devices.\n\n---- Out of scope ------\n- End-to-end encryption.\n- Search functionality within chats.\n- Voice and video calling.\n- Complex user presence (e.g., \"last seen at\").\n\n2) Scale of the System: \n- 1B+ Monthly Active Users (MAU).\n- 100K+ concurrent messages/sec across large chat rooms.\n\n3) Non Functional Requirements (SPARCS):  \n- Scalability: Support 1B+ MAU, 100K+ concurrent messages/sec.\n- Performance: P95 end-to-end message delivery latency < 200ms.\n- Availability: CAP-Aware Messaging Guarantees (prioritize availability,\nenforce strong per-chat ordering).\n- Reliability: Message Durability (persist before ack; zero acknowledged\nmessage loss).\n- Consistency: Consistent Multi-Device state (P95 sync < 300ms, <1%\nread/notification inconsistency).\n\n------- Out of Scope --------\n- Advanced spam detection and automated content moderation.\n- Complex analytics pipelines and administrative dashboards.\n\n4) BOE Calculations: \n- Load / Traffic (QPS)\n    > DAU = 500M, 5:1(R:W)\n    > Read QPS: 5*(500M DAU)/ (10^5) => 25k QPS\n    > Write QPS: 5k QPS\n    > Peak QPS: (X3) ≈ 90k QPS\n\n- Storage\n    > Daily storage = 500M writes × 1 KB average request => 500 GB\n    > Yearly storage = 500 GB × 365 => 182.5 TB\n    > Total storage = 182.5 TB × 5 => 912.5 TB\n    > replication ≈ 912.5 TB × 3 => 2.73 PB\n\n- Bandwidth\n    > Ingress = 5,000 write QPS × 1 KB average write => 5 MB/s\n    > Egress = 25,000 read QPS × 1 KB average read => 25 MB/s\n\n- Cache \n    > 2.5B daily read requests × 1 KB × 0.20 = 500GB\n-- We could add a factor of 100 for all given we are allowing media files\nwhich are huge in size. But again media is mostly stored in S3. \n\n5) Core Entities \n- User\n- Chat\n- Message\n- Media\n- DeviceSession\n\n\n6) API Design \n\nPOST/media/upload  \n    Input: {mediaFile, metadata}\n    Output: 2xx, success (mediaUrl)\n\nGET/chat/:chatId/messages -- historical messages \n    Input: {cursor, limit}\n    Output: {messageList, nextCursor}\n\nCRUD for Group/Members\n\n> send_message: Client -> Server | User sends a message to a chat\n> new_message: Server -> Clients | Fan-out of message to all\nparticipants\n> message_deleted: Server -> Clients | Notify when a message is deleted\n> user_typing: Client -> Server | Typing indicator (debounced)\n> typing_started / typing_stopped: Server -> Clients | Render live\ntyping indicators\n> read_receipt: Client -> Server | User read a message\npresence_update: Server -> Clients | Updates about online/offline\nstatus\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n1) Functional Requirements:  \n- Users can send and receive messages in 1:1 and group chats (ordered, persistent history).\n- Messages support rich media (images, videos, files).\n- Users receive real-time in-app and push notifications for new messages.\n- Users can delete their own messages, reflecting across all devices.\n\n---- Out of scope ------\n- End-to-end encryption.\n- Search functionality within chats.\n- Voice and video calling.\n- Complex user presence (e.g., \"last seen at\").\n\n2) Scale of the System: \n- 1B+ Monthly Active Users (MAU).\n- 100K+ concurrent messages/sec across large chat rooms.\n\n3) Non Functional Requirements (SPARCS):  \n- Scalability: Support 1B+ MAU, 100K+ concurrent messages/sec.\n- Performance: P95 end-to-end message delivery latency < 200ms.\n- Availability: CAP-Aware Messaging Guarantees (prioritize availability, enforce strong per-chat ordering).\n- Reliability: Message Durability (persist before ack; zero acknowledged message loss).\n- Consistency: Consistent Multi-Device state (P95 sync < 300ms, <1% read/notification inconsistency).\n\n------- Out of Scope --------\n- Advanced spam detection and automated content moderation.\n- Complex analytics pipelines and administrative dashboards.\n\n4) BOE Calculations: \n- Load / Traffic (QPS)\n    > DAU = 500M, 5:1(R:W)\n    > Read QPS: 5*(500M DAU)/ (10^5) => 25k QPS\n    > Write QPS: 5k QPS\n    > Peak QPS: (X3) ≈ 90k QPS\n\n- Storage\n    > Daily storage = 500M writes × 1 KB average request => 500 GB\n    > Yearly storage = 500 GB × 365 => 182.5 TB\n    > Total storage = 182.5 TB × 5 => 912.5 TB\n    > replication ≈ 912.5 TB × 3 => 2.73 PB\n\n- Bandwidth\n    > Ingress = 5,000 write QPS × 1 KB average write => 5 MB/s\n    > Egress = 25,000 read QPS × 1 KB average read => 25 MB/s\n\n- Cache \n    > 2.5B daily read requests × 1 KB × 0.20 = 500GB\n-- We could add a factor of 100 for all given we are allowing media files which are huge in size. But again media is mostly stored in S3. \n\n5) Core Entities \n- User\n- Chat\n- Message\n- Media\n- DeviceSession\n\n\n6) API Design \n\nPOST/media/upload  \n    Input: {mediaFile, metadata}\n    Output: 2xx, success (mediaUrl)\n\nGET/chat/:chatId/messages -- historical messages \n    Input: {cursor, limit}\n    Output: {messageList, nextCursor}\n\nCRUD for Group/Members\n\n> send_message: Client -> Server | User sends a message to a chat\n> new_message: Server -> Clients | Fan-out of message to all participants\n> message_deleted: Server -> Clients | Notify when a message is deleted\n> user_typing: Client -> Server | Typing indicator (debounced)\n> typing_started / typing_stopped: Server -> Clients | Render live typing indicators\n> read_receipt: Client -> Server | User read a message\npresence_update: Server -> Clients | Updates about online/offline status\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
